{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createAsyncRateLimiter<TFn, TSelected>(\n   host,\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): LitAsyncRateLimiter<TFn, TSelected>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/lit-pacer/src/async-rate-limiter/createAsyncRateLimiter.ts#L96","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async-rate-limiter/createAsyncRateLimiter.ts:96"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates and retains the AsyncRateLimiter for its Lit owner."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accepts at most a configured number of calls in a fixed or sliding window. Calls beyond the limit are rejected rather than queued. Use the state and timing methods to display capacity and retry timing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The callback may return a Promise. Core result, error, retry, and abort behavior is preserved.\nUse onSuccess, onError, and onSettled for execution outcomes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-and-subscriptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State and subscriptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a selector to track only the state consumed by the owner. The default selection is {},\nso utility state changes do not update the owner unless it opts in. Selection uses shallow\ncomparison. The raw store remains available for additional subscriptions.\nUse utility.subscribe(childHost, selector) for a child subscription. It returns a getter\nand cleans up with the child without canceling the parent utility."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available state fields:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have resulted in errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionTimes"},{"type":"text","value":": Array of timestamps when executions occurred for rate limiting calculations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isExceeded"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the rate limiter has exceeded the limit"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isExecuting"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the rate-limited function is currently executing asynchronously"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastResult"},{"type":"text","value":": The result from the most recent successful function execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rejectionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have been rejected due to rate limiting"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"settleCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have completed (either successfully or with errors)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current execution status - 'disabled' when not active, 'executing' when executing, 'idle' when not executing, 'exceeded' when rate limit is exceeded"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"successCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have completed successfully"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maybeExecuteCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of times maybeExecute has been called (for reduction calculations)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options-and-ownership","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options and ownership"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass an options object with property getters or a factory. Top-level properties are read\nreactively; function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider\ndefaults. Updates retain the utility, its store, counters, and pending work.\nDisconnecting the host calls abort().\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the same adapter instance. A custom callback\nmust perform all required cleanup. Use flush() where supported to finish pending work.\nReconnecting the host refreshes options and restores subscriptions to the same instance."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyAsyncFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"host","children":[{"type":"text","value":"host"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactiveControllerHost"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owner of option updates, subscriptions, and cleanup."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function executed by the utility."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/LitPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/LitAsyncRateLimiterOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitAsyncRateLimiterOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core options or a reactive factory, plus an optional onUnmount callback."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selects state that updates the owner. Omit to leave selected state empty."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/LitAsyncRateLimiter.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitAsyncRateLimiter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The retained utility instance with selected state and child subscriptions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createAsyncRateLimiter } from '@tanstack/lit-pacer'\n\nconst utility = createAsyncRateLimiter(\n  this, async (value: string) => { console.log(value) },\n  { limit: 5, window: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount }),\n)\nutility.maybeExecute('item')\n// Selected state: utility.state.executionCount","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-and-subscriptions","text":"State and subscriptions","level":2},{"id":"options-and-ownership","text":"Options and ownership","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"host","text":"host","level":3},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createAsyncRateLimiter<TFn, TSelected>(\n   host,\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): LitAsyncRateLimiter<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-rate-limiter/createAsyncRateLimiter.ts:96](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/lit-pacer/src/async-rate-limiter/createAsyncRateLimiter.ts#L96)\n\nCreates and retains the AsyncRateLimiter for its Lit owner.\n\nAccepts at most a configured number of calls in a fixed or sliding window. Calls beyond the limit are rejected rather than queued. Use the state and timing methods to display capacity and retry timing.\n\nThe callback may return a Promise. Core result, error, retry, and abort behavior is preserved.\nUse onSuccess, onError, and onSettled for execution outcomes.\n\n## State and subscriptions\n\nPass a selector to track only the state consumed by the owner. The default selection is {},\nso utility state changes do not update the owner unless it opts in. Selection uses shallow\ncomparison. The raw store remains available for additional subscriptions.\nUse utility.subscribe(childHost, selector) for a child subscription. It returns a getter\nand cleans up with the child without canceling the parent utility.\n\nAvailable state fields:\n\n- `errorCount`: Number of function executions that have resulted in errors\n- `executionTimes`: Array of timestamps when executions occurred for rate limiting calculations\n- `isExceeded`: Whether the rate limiter has exceeded the limit\n- `isExecuting`: Whether the rate-limited function is currently executing asynchronously\n- `lastResult`: The result from the most recent successful function execution\n- `rejectionCount`: Number of function executions that have been rejected due to rate limiting\n- `settleCount`: Number of function executions that have completed (either successfully or with errors)\n- `status`: Current execution status - 'disabled' when not active, 'executing' when executing, 'idle' when not executing, 'exceeded' when rate limit is exceeded\n- `successCount`: Number of function executions that have completed successfully\n- `maybeExecuteCount`: Number of times maybeExecute has been called (for reduction calculations)\n\n## Options and ownership\n\nPass an options object with property getters or a factory. Top-level properties are read\nreactively; function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider\ndefaults. Updates retain the utility, its store, counters, and pending work.\nDisconnecting the host calls abort().\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the same adapter instance. A custom callback\nmust perform all required cleanup. Use flush() where supported to finish pending work.\nReconnecting the host refreshes options and restores subscriptions to the same instance.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### host\n\n`ReactiveControllerHost`\n\nOwner of option updates, subscriptions, and cleanup.\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\nFunction executed by the utility.\n\n### options\n\n[`LitPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/LitPacerOptions.md)\\<[`LitAsyncRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/LitAsyncRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\nCore options or a reactive factory, plus an optional onUnmount callback.\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\nSelects state that updates the owner. Omit to leave selected state empty.\n\n## Returns\n\n[`LitAsyncRateLimiter`](../interfaces/LitAsyncRateLimiter.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\nThe retained utility instance with selected state and child subscriptions.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { createAsyncRateLimiter } from '@tanstack/lit-pacer'\n\nconst utility = createAsyncRateLimiter(\n  this, async (value: string) => { console.log(value) },\n  { limit: 5, window: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount }),\n)\nutility.maybeExecute('item')\n// Selected state: utility.state.executionCount\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createAsyncRateLimiter\ntitle: createAsyncRateLimiter\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createAsyncRateLimiter<TFn, TSelected>(\n   host,\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): LitAsyncRateLimiter<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-rate-limiter/createAsyncRateLimiter.ts:96](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/lit-pacer/src/async-rate-limiter/createAsyncRateLimiter.ts#L96)\n\nCreates and retains the AsyncRateLimiter for its Lit owner.\n\nAccepts at most a configured number of calls in a fixed or sliding window. Calls beyond the limit are rejected rather than queued. Use the state and timing methods to display capacity and retry timing.\n\nThe callback may return a Promise. Core result, error, retry, and abort behavior is preserved.\nUse onSuccess, onError, and onSettled for execution outcomes.\n\n## State and subscriptions\n\nPass a selector to track only the state consumed by the owner. The default selection is {},\nso utility state changes do not update the owner unless it opts in. Selection uses shallow\ncomparison. The raw store remains available for additional subscriptions.\nUse utility.subscribe(childHost, selector) for a child subscription. It returns a getter\nand cleans up with the child without canceling the parent utility.\n\nAvailable state fields:\n\n- `errorCount`: Number of function executions that have resulted in errors\n- `executionTimes`: Array of timestamps when executions occurred for rate limiting calculations\n- `isExceeded`: Whether the rate limiter has exceeded the limit\n- `isExecuting`: Whether the rate-limited function is currently executing asynchronously\n- `lastResult`: The result from the most recent successful function execution\n- `rejectionCount`: Number of function executions that have been rejected due to rate limiting\n- `settleCount`: Number of function executions that have completed (either successfully or with errors)\n- `status`: Current execution status - 'disabled' when not active, 'executing' when executing, 'idle' when not executing, 'exceeded' when rate limit is exceeded\n- `successCount`: Number of function executions that have completed successfully\n- `maybeExecuteCount`: Number of times maybeExecute has been called (for reduction calculations)\n\n## Options and ownership\n\nPass an options object with property getters or a factory. Top-level properties are read\nreactively; function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider\ndefaults. Updates retain the utility, its store, counters, and pending work.\nDisconnecting the host calls abort().\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the same adapter instance. A custom callback\nmust perform all required cleanup. Use flush() where supported to finish pending work.\nReconnecting the host refreshes options and restores subscriptions to the same instance.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### host\n\n`ReactiveControllerHost`\n\nOwner of option updates, subscriptions, and cleanup.\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\nFunction executed by the utility.\n\n### options\n\n[`LitPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/LitPacerOptions.md)\\<[`LitAsyncRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/LitAsyncRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\nCore options or a reactive factory, plus an optional onUnmount callback.\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\nSelects state that updates the owner. Omit to leave selected state empty.\n\n## Returns\n\n[`LitAsyncRateLimiter`](../interfaces/LitAsyncRateLimiter.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\nThe retained utility instance with selected state and child subscriptions.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { createAsyncRateLimiter } from '@tanstack/lit-pacer'\n\nconst utility = createAsyncRateLimiter(\n  this, async (value: string) => { console.log(value) },\n  { limit: 5, window: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount }),\n)\nutility.maybeExecute('item')\n// Selected state: utility.state.executionCount\n```\n"}
